This log depicts a successful brute-force attack followed by a malicious session on a compromised server. An attacker from IP address 203.0.113.45 attempted multiple failed SSH login attempts for the "root" user before successfully authenticating as the "backup" user. During the session, the attacker used `sudo` to execute commands such as `wget` to download a script from an external IP, `chmod` to make it executable, and `bash` to run it. The script executed malicious commands, including creating a new user named "sysupd" with UID 0 (root privileges), modifying `/etc/passwd` and `/etc/shadow`, and creating a cron job in `/etc/cron.d/sysupd`. Finally, the attacker deleted their history file (`/home/backup/.bash_history`) before terminating the session.

